    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's what I changed and why.\n\n## Summary\n\nReplaced the string `membershipTier` with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133), computed on the DTO and recorded in the create audit line.\n\n**Level formula:** start at 1; `+1` when email present; `+1` when `namesakeCount == 0`; `min(\u2026, 3)` (level 4 reserved for tenure).\n\n**Files touched (5):**\n1. `openapi.yml` \u2014 replaced the `membershipTier` (string) schema with `membershipLevel` (integer, 1\u20133, readOnly). This regenerates `OwnerDto` with `get/setMembershipLevel(Integer)`.\n2. `OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 swapped the one `@Mapping` expression from the SILVER/BRONZE string to the numeric level.\n3. `RespondWithOwner.java` / `RespondWithOwnerCreated.java` \u2014 removed the now-defunct `GOLD` tier override (it set `membershipTier`, which no longer exists), dropping the unused `OwnerRepository`/`HouseholdTier` dependency.\n4. `AuditOwnerCreated.java` \u2014 the create audit line now records `membershipLevel` instead of the tier.\n\n## Keeping structural impact low\n- The level formula lives in **one place** (the mapper expression); the audit reuses it via `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner).getMembershipLevel()` rather than duplicating the logic \u2014 so no new class and no branching added to the audit method (it stays CC 1).\n- The `RespondWith*` edits *remove* a branch each rather than grow the methods.\n- I left the now-unused `HouseholdTier` class untouched (it compiles fine) to avoid touching an extra file \u2014 GOLD/household tiers aren't part of the new spec.\n\n**Result:** `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`. The audit log confirms `membershipLevel=3` for an owner with an email and a unique name (`1 + email + namesake0`, capped at 3), matching the acceptance test.",
